      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 640871472,
      "version": 275,
      "versionNonce": 1373636706,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779305764761,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Exercise 3.16: Ben Bitdiddle decides to write a procedure to count the number\nof pairs in any list structure. “It’s easy,” he reasons. “The number of pairs in any\nstructure is the number in the car plus the number in the cdr plus one more to count\nthe current pair.” So Ben writes the following procedure:\n\n(define (count-pairs x)\n    (if (not (pair? x))\n        0\n        (+ (count-pairs (car x)) (count-pairs (cdr x)) 1)))\n\nShow that this procedure is not correct. In particular, draw box-and-pointer diagrams\nrepresenting list structures made up of exactly three pairs for which Ben’s procedure\nwould return 3; return 4; return 7; never return at all.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Exercise 3.16: Ben Bitdiddle decides to write a procedure to count the number\nof pairs in any list structure. “It’s easy,” he reasons. “The number of pairs in any\nstructure is the number in the car plus the number in the cdr plus one more to count\nthe current pair.” So Ben writes the following procedure:\n\n(define (count-pairs x)\n    (if (not (pair? x))\n        0\n        (+ (count-pairs (car x)) (count-pairs (cdr x)) 1)))\n\nShow that this procedure is not correct. In particular, draw box-and-pointer diagrams\nrepresenting list structures made up of exactly three pairs for which Ben’s procedure\nwould return 3; return 4; return 7; never return at all.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
